# Keep USB autosuspend off for the TP-Link RTL8822BU Wi-Fi adapter.
#
# The chip's own IPS (Inactive Power Save) state is the thing that wedges it,
# and USB-level autosuspend is a second, independent way for the link to go
# quiet. The device currently reads power/control=on, but that is not sticky:
# after a re-enumeration (including the ones this watchdog performs) it reverts
# to the bus default, which is `auto`. This rule makes it stick.
#
# Belt-and-braces, not the primary fix — disabling Wi-Fi power save in
# NetworkManager is what actually stops the wedge. See README.md.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="2357", ATTR{idProduct}=="0138", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
